  "text": "Gold Price in the 1960s\nBetween the first (1968-04-30) and last (1969-12-31) monthly observations available for the 1960s, the LBMA gold price went from $39.10 to $35.20 — a decline of 10% — with a sampled high of $43.60 (Apr 1969) and a sampled low of $35.20 (Dec 1969).\nYears in the 1960s\n1968\n1969\nSee today's live gold price on the\nspot dashboard\n, or\nshop gold bullion\nat Bullion Trading LLC.\nData retrieved 2026-09-26. Latest observation for this metal: 2026-09-25. The current month is provisional.\nSources, sampling and calculation methodology\n.\nPrepared by the\nBullion Trading LLC editorial team\n.",
